+## Storage and deploys
 
-Sessions live in Postgres ([keep sessions in the database](../adr/0001-keep-sessions-in-the-database.md)).
+The browser holds the member identifier and expiry in a signed cookie; there is no server-side session store, and
+the old Postgres session table has been dropped. The implementation above signs cookies and verifies their
+signature and expiry before returning the member identifier. Signing protects integrity; the cookie contents are
+not encrypted.
+
+Every web server must use the same `LARDER_SESSION_KEY` from deploy secrets. Keep that key across deploys so existing
+cookies remain valid on every server. The implementation's `dev-only` fallback is for development; deployments
+must supply the shared secret.
+
+## Known limits
+
+- A member's session cannot be revoked individually from the server before its cookie expires. The expiry in
+  [Lifetime](#lifetime) bounds the validity of an issued cookie; there is no immediate individual revocation
+  mechanism.
+- Rotating the signing key logs everyone out. Rotate it only between pickups to avoid disrupting pickup.
 
